lass=3D"QuestionText"><p>Establishing and testing a theory is a systematic =
approach to diagnosing a problem. By identifying probable
causes and confirming them through testing, technicians can efficiently det=
ermine the root cause and proceed
with an appropriate solution.</p>
<p>It is important to diagnose the problem before implementing a solution. =
Skipping the step of establishing and
testing a theory could lead to incorrect fixes and wasted effort.</p>
<p>It is also important to go beyond symptoms and identify the underlying c=
auses of the problem. Focusing only on
symptoms without testing theories would result in incomplete troubleshootin=
g.</p>
<p>The troubleshooting process encourages using research techniques, consul=
ting other technicians, and leveraging
external resources when necessary. Collaboration and research are valuable =
tools for accurately diagnosing and
resolving issues.</p></div></div><div id=3D"ExamEngine-references" class=3D=
